### Get UTC hours from Date objects with time zone offsets in JavaScript

Source: https://github.com/mdn/content/blob/main/files/en-us/web/javascript/reference/global_objects/date/getutchours/index.md

This example demonstrates how the `getUTCHours()` method retrieves the UTC hour component from `Date` objects, illustrating its behavior with different time zone offsets. It initializes two `Date` objects with distinct GMT offsets and logs their respective UTC hours, showing how the method normalizes to UTC.

```javascript
const date1 = new Date("December 31, 1975, 23:15:30 GMT+11:00");
const date2 = new Date("December 31, 1975, 23:15:30 GMT-11:00");

console.log(date1.getUTCHours());
// Expected output: 12

console.log(date2.getUTCHours());
// Expected output: 10
```

